Yep, there are no more challenges left in life for me - I ascended a
hobbit Tourist in Slash'EM.

This after my last ascendable character - another hobbit Tourist -
died to Pestilence when my blessed +6 unicorn horn failed me.  (I made
a number of other errors, but they would've been forgiven if the horn
hadn't crapped out when I was ill.)

The game seemed to kind of give up and give me a pass on this game at
some point around Grund's or so.  It's like the RNG just decided, "Eh,
why not just let him win one?"

I found Disrupter on a bones pile.  I never really understood how one
was supposed to deal with L's and esp. Vecna until the first time I
got Disrupter.  The Chaotic Quest becomes a walk in the park with it.

Grayswandir was in a shop - my pets helped me to it.  (Yes, it's
Lawful, but the blasting damage is totally worth it to have the proper
tool for Gehennom and Demogorgon.)

The Lady smiled on me and gave me Mirrorbright early, as well as
Vorpal Blade, which is the proper tool for most non-undead, non-demon
problems.  She did give me the crappy Ogresmasher, but at least didn't
bother with Giantkiller (saw it in a shop), Trollsbane (never saw it),
or the Brands (took +6 Fire Brand off a Yeoman on Astral).  Also no
Gauntlets of Defense this time, which was good, as I found gauntlets
of dexterity early on.

I managed the endgame with my usual combination of wands of death
(recharged via PYEC) and a +5 submachine gun with a few hundred rounds
of +7 ammo.

I don't remember when I found the first one, but I ended up with two
wands of wishing long before the Castle, plus I found an extra magic
lamp beyond the Sunless Sea one, AND got two throne wishes.  It was
silly.  I had more than a dozen wishes available when I ascended.  The
eight I used were mostly for convenience after the first (cloak of
MR):  healthstone (later found 3 more), touchstone (much later found
another), helm of brilliance (never found another), deep dragon scale
mail (didn't get dropped deep scales for a loooong time), amulet of
water breathing (doesn't exist, so got another flying instead), amulet
of magical breathing (never found another), and a magic whistle (found
another long after my pets had been decimated).

I didn't bother with Ludios, as I heard it's just a big tourist trap.

I don't remember ever being in terrible danger, though I did have to
Elbereth a few times (other than Vecna & Demogorgon, natch), and it
was a slog getting through the graveyard to retrieve the amulet.  I
killed Rodney at least a half dozen times there, and they were messy,
as he kept Double-Troubling over and over and one of them grabbed my
PYEC so I had to machine gun a bunch as I was never sure which one was
magic-resistant.

My last time through it was getting up into double-digits the number
of times that something cast that damn 'pool of water' spell at me on
non-teleport levels.  I now consider an amulet of either flying or
magical breathing to be a requirement for ascension, and important to
obtain ASAP.  I don't think anyone tried it on me this time, though.
I also really like the ring of free action (Suck it, nightgaunts and
shades!) and prefer deep dragon scale mail for amulet-less drain
resistance.  (Though last time through Rodney stole the PYEC that was
providing my ONLY magic resistance the first time I met him; that was
ugly, and now I go for the cloak for redundancy.)

I remembered to put on my +2 ring of adornment before ascending, but
forgot to pop my figurine of a blue dragon to have a pet.  (My angel
went peaceful after the last several rounds of a burst that put down
Death went into her.)  So only half style points, though I should get
something for being expert in dart and short sword, for cthulhusakes!

All in all, pretty straightforward.  Can I have my key to the
executive washroom now?

Thanks,
